"open":{"tax":"Patches 0, 4, 10, 12, 13, 14 need the corrections given. Separately, L106 'Zürich, Bern, Aargau, Schwyz: NO Liegenschaftssteuer' is wrong for Bern: Bern communes may levy a Liegenschaftssteuer of at most 1.5 per mille of the amtlicher Wert (Art. 258 ff. StG BE; taxinfo.sv.fin.be.ch 'Liegenschaftssteuer', Fassung 29 Jan 2026; sv.fin.be.ch Bernisches Steuerrecht 2024 Art. 261). Other unsourced, unlabelled lines remain: L107 'Most cantons: low to moderate' (ch.ch says more than half the cantons levy 0.1-3 per mille), L115 alpine second-home tax prediction, L157 reinvestment exemption, L163 'Wealth tax rates stable'.","cost benchmark":"Rows 16 and 18 need the corrections given. The closed note covers only the transaction rows; GEAK 800-1,500, Asbestsanierung, Energetische Sanierung, Erdbebenverstärkung, Permafrost and Alpine roof rows carry no source or est. label.","rental":"Lines 185-188 still carry unsourced claims ('Geneva: max 90 days/yr without commercial license', patente cantonale in Genève/Vaud/Zürich, 'Zürich: tightening 2024-2025'); and confirmed line 2's 'point 1' and 'RK-S' are not on its listed pages (the Voting URL selects only decisions; the Business record says only 'In Kommission des Ständerats' since 22 Sep 2026).","work":"The Mindestlohn line gives cantonal hourly minima (Genève, Basel-Stadt, Jura, Neuchâtel, Ticino) with no source link and no est. label; Genève CHF 24.59 matches ge.ch, the others were not checked."}}
